<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    Tauri merges this Info.plist into the bundled macOS app. Each TCC service
    Daisy touches needs its own usage string, or the OS denies it (feeding
    zeros) or kills the process instead of prompting:
      - NSMicrophoneUsageDescription  -> AVAudioEngine mic input (the room).
      - NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription -> Core Audio process tap for the system
        audio mix (the remote side). Verified on hardware: without this key the
        tap is granted-but-silent. No screen-recording consent is needed.
      - NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription -> the CoreBluetooth peripheral that
        wakes a paired phone. Without this key the first CBPeripheralManager
        is a SIGKILL, not a denial.
  -->
  <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Daisy records your microphone so it can transcribe and summarize your meetings. Audio stays on your device.</string>
  <key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Daisy records this computer's audio (the people you're meeting with) so it can transcribe and summarize your meetings. Audio stays on your device.</string>
  <key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
  <string>Daisy uses Bluetooth to wake your paired phone when a recording is ready for it. Your meetings stay on your devices.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
